**Step 3. The `needs-kam` rule, then re-label the 18.**
**The rule (write it in the seed log, JIRA.md-style, and in the C-entry):** `needs-kam` stays ONLY on an issue whose next step genuinely waits on the product owner TODAY: a decision or act that is his alone and that no ruling, hold or card already settles. It is REMOVED when (a) the owner already ruled it (C-entry, or his ruling of a named date), (b) the issue is stale or superseded, (c) the next step is an ops or design call the coordinator can make, or (d) the next step is another person's (the reviewer's answer, a reviewer round that has not ended).
- Ruled **hold** (a hold or park ruling, or "after the reviewer's current round"): remove `needs-kam`, add `held`, comment citing the C-entry and ruling (see the text rule: "the product owner's ruling of 2026-10-23" for the 2026-10-23 rulings; for C-71 rulings the C-number and COMP number are allowed).
- Ruled stale/superseded/ops-or-design-call: remove `needs-kam`; ONE comment line naming the reason. Do not close, transition or edit anything else.
- Drafter's expectation (check each row whole; you may differ, state why): #1, #17 stale (remove, comment); #26, #27, #84, #171, #247, #319 ops or design calls the coordinator can make (remove, comment; read #319 whole first, its State says "until the project owner has seen it" and an owner look may be a genuine ask: keep it with a one-line reason if so); #249 held (mapping review ruled `b` today: remove, add `held`, comment "the product owner's ruling of 2026-10-23: hold until the reviewer's current round ends"); #265 (same mapping/SME-check line, C-57): decide by reading, likely held with #249; #333 (the five questions): the note is with the product owner and he will send it, but the next step after that is the reviewer's answer (Q-P1) — read it, decide, justify; #330, #336 to #339, #347, #366: read each whole, apply the rule; keep `needs-kam` where the owner's review, confirmation or word is the genuine next step and nothing rules it.
- Each change is a Jira write on PCOMP only: `PUT /rest/api/3/issue/<key>` with `update.labels` add/remove (never replace the full label set), comment `POST /rest/api/3/issue/<key>/comment` in Atlassian document format. **Print the before and after label set per issue** (a table into STATUS and the seed log); read back every issue (labels equal the plan; a one-character mutant compares unequal). The idempotency labels `composer-seed-1023` and `plan-comp-<row#>` must survive on every issue (assert by program, 67 of 67). Final counts by JQL: `needs-kam` n, `held` h; reconcile with the table. Write the plan table BEFORE the first write to `.tools/b521/scratch/plan-labels.json`.

**Step 4. The 32 AMBIGUOUS rows.** Read each row's State and item text whole. Classify **OPEN** (seed it) or **CLOSED** (not seeded; one line why). Print the table `row, class, one-line reason` into STATUS and the seed log.
