- OPEN: a stated next step remains. That includes rows carrying "Ruled 2026-10-12 (C-71 ..." hold or park text (#35, #55 COMP-2; #54, #73, #101 COMP-17; #227 COMP-16; #228, #231 COMP-2; #252 COMP-1 (b); others): a hold keeps the work open, so they are OPEN, seeded WITH `held` and WITHOUT `needs-kam`, the comment/description naming the ruling by its C- and COMP- ids. #329 (the five questions): the ruling is made and the note is with the product owner; the send to the reviewer is still his act: OPEN, seeded WITH `needs-kam` and a first-line description note that the note reached him on 2026-10-23 (no card id, no name). Rows with no ruling and an owner's word or call as next step (#30, #104, #106, #158, #223, #226, #236, #240, #272 etc.): read them; label `needs-kam` only if the rule of Step 3 holds, else no extra label.
